  speakerName: Rayo
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'Now let''s learn the opposite direction.

    In Ilokano, ''umay''
    means ''come.''

    You can use it when asking someone to move toward you or
    toward a particular place.

    Listen carefully: umay.

    Now, try saying
    ''umay'' yourself.'
